            "review_title": "Review at Sóno Grill & Bar",
            "review_text": "1926yanks\nSeattle, Washington753 contributions\n0\nHip, Creative, and Tasty\nFeb 2023 • Friends\nThis restaurant is in an off-the-beaten track location in District 2, but is well worth finding. It reminds me of a chic urban restaurant in the US, with an open kitchen, backlit bar, and jazz wafting thru the air. \nCocktail were colorful & creative. The dishes were plated with a flourish & even better to eat. We started with a snapper ceviche, served in a lime & cream sauce and bone marrow with mustard seeds & caramalized onions\nThe aged duck breast with Cora dẻ & hot pepper (&!pickled papaya) was wonderful. I was most surprised by the king prawns with homemade pasta (pasta was the dish I most missed during my VN travel!) the pasta was Al dente & excellent! \nGracious service. The entire experience was a Foodie’s delight.\nRead more\nWritten February 18, 2023",
